$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Procedure A: Stoichiometric acetalization. To a mixture of the carbonyl
compound (1.5 mmol) in MeOH (HPLC grade, 5 mL), hydroxylamine
hydrochloride (2.25 mmol) and lithium carbonate (2.25 mmol) were added in
that order. The reaction was stirred for 30 min, then 3 mL of saturated
NH4Cl and 3 mL of H2O were added. The mixture was extracted with diethyl
ether (3 x 10 mL); the combined organic layers were washed with brine (10
mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated by rotary evaporation. Benzaldehyde
dimethyl acetal 2a. Stoichiometric procedure: Benzaldehyde (1.0 mL, 9.5
mmol) was dissolved in MeOH (31.4 mL) and reacted with hydroxylamine
hydrochloride (0.990 g, 14.3 mmol) and lithium carbonate (1.05 g, 14.4
mmol) according to procedure A above. The acetal (1.20 g, 83%) was
isolated as a clear, colorless oil. 1H NMR, 13C NMR, and IR spectra
correlated with those for the authentic compound.[i]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield, optimized on amount of
base and hydroxylamine hydrochloride, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Method for the selective formation of dimethyl acetals in the presence of
hydroxylamine
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
