$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the synthesis of hexaoxonanes from acetals 1a-h and
dihydroperoxides 2a-d Acetal 1a-h (2.6 mmol) was added to a solution of
dihydroperoxide 2a-d (2 mmol) in 1.5 mL of Et2O for 2a - 2с; 8-10 mL of
THF for 2d. A solution of boron trifluoride etherate (0.2-0.6 mol of BF3
• Et2O per mole of 2) in diethyl ether (0.5 mL) (in the reactions with
2a-c) or THF (0.5 mL) (in the reaction with 2d) was added to the reaction
mixture at 0-5 ⁰С (in the reaction with 2a), 20 ⁰С (in the reaction with
2b - d). Then the mixtures were stirred at 20-25 ⁰С (in the reaction with
2a - d) for 3-8 h, or 55-60 ⁰С (in the reaction with 2d) for 1-5 h.
15,15-Dimethyl-6,7,13,14,16,17-hexaoxadispiro[4.2.4.5]heptadecane (3a),
yield 82% White crystals Mp = 64 – 66 °C. Rf 0.38 (TLC, hexane – EA,
20:1). 1Н NMR (250.13 MHz), δ: 1.25-1.40 (br.s, 6H), 1.45-1.70 (m, 12H),
1.94-2.14 (m, 4H). 13С NMR (62.9 MHz), δ: 21.1, 24.2, 33.0, 107.4, 118.5.
Anal. Calcd for C13H22O6: C, 56.92; H, 8.08. Found: C, 56.71; H, 8.48
