$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of 7,7-Dimethoxyalkanoate Methyl
Esters 9a-c and Cycloalkanone Derivatives 5a, 6d-f, 7a, 8a; General
Procedure: Trimethyl orthoformate (16.4 mL, 150 mmol) and
p-toluenesulfonic acid (0.15g, 0.78 mmol) in dry methanol (30 mL) were
added to an Erlenmeyer flask (250 mL) with 2-acyl cycloalkanone 1-4 (100
mmol) and the mixture was kept for 24 hours at room temperature (25-30
°C). The mixture was neutralized with sodium carbonate and filtered. The
solvent was removed in vacuo and products 5a, 6d-f, 7a, 8a, 9a-c were
purified by distillation, (see Table). 6d, yield 82%. Bp/ mBar: 75/25°C;
1H NMR δ: 3.50 (H2), 1.35 - 2.0 -(CH2)4-, 3.08, 3.15 (OMe1); 13C NMR δ,
44.7 (C2), 25.2 (C3), 19.9 (C4), 21.8 (C5), 29.1 (C6), 191.1 (C7), 115.4
(C8), 47.7,47.3 (OMe1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Regiochemistry of the reaction of 2-acylcyclohexanones with trimethyl
orthoformate. A convenient one-pot method to obtain
7,7-dimethoxyalkanoate methyl esters
