$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The PPG reagent and the aldehyde (PPG/aldehyde
= 1:2) were stirred at 140 °C under argon for 2 h. Upon completion, the
reaction mixtures were purified by flash column chromatography to afford
the desired acetals.
6-Methoxy-4,4-bis(3-methoxy-phenyl)-2-phenethyl-4H-benzo[1,3]dioxine (4),
yield 82%. Rf 0.3 (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate = 7/1); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.31 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.18-7.24 (m, 3 H), 7.11-7.15 (m, 1
H), 7.07-7.09 (m, 2 H), 6.91-6.96 (m, 2 H), 6.78-6.86 (m, 6 H), 6.41 (d,
J = 2.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.92 (dd, J = 4.1, 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 3.72 (s, 3 H), 3.70
(s, 3 H), 3.60 (s, 3 H), 2.80 (ddd, J = 5.8, 9.8, 14.1 Hz, 1 H), 2.64
(ddd, J = 7.2, 9.3, 14.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.04-2.21 (m, 2 H); 13C NMR (101 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 159.3, 159.1, 152.8, 147.3, 146.3, 145.7, 141.4, 128.9, 128.7,
128.27, 128.23, 125.7, 125.6, 121.8, 120.6, 117.5, 115.0, 114.8, 114.2,
114.0, 113.2, 112.4, 94.5, 84.0, 55.5, 55.1, 55.1, 36.1, 29.6; IR(neat)
3000, 2936, 2833, 1598, 1493, 1256, 1225, 1196, 1126, 814, 700; HRMS
(ESI) m/e calcd for C31H30O5Na, 505.1991, found 505.1999.
