$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3,5-Dinitroacetophenone dimethyl ketalwas prepared from
3,5-dinitroacetophenone by modifying the method used to prepare
4-methoxyacetophenone dimethyl ketal. 3,5- Dinitroacetophenone (1.05 g, 5
mmol), trimethylorthoformate (0.5306 g, 5 mmol), methanol (1 mL), and
p-toluenesulfonic acid (5 mg) were mixed and the reaction mixture was
stirred for three days. The solid crystalline product was collected by
filtration, washed with cold methanol, dried under vacuum, and used
directly without further purification (81% yield).
3,5-Dinitroacetophenone dimethyl ketal , yield 81% 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 1.58 (3H, s, CH3), 3.22 (6H, s, OCH3), 8.68 (2H, d, J = 2.0 Hz,
Ar), 8.98 (1H, s, Ar). UV (λmax): 236 nm (ε 21 000 M-1 cm-1). Anal.
(C10H12O6N2) C, H, N.
