$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Acetal Formation
Caution: Diazides are potential explosives and should be handled with
care and all necessary protective measures should be taken during the
reaction. To an oven dried 15 mL round-bottom flask equipped with a
magnetic stirring bar was added 0.3 mmol of aldehyde, 0.3 mmol of
2-aryl-2-azidoethanol, 5 mL of dry dichloromethane and 5 mol% of
Cu(OTf)2. The reaction mixture was refluxed overnight. The reaction
mixture was diluted with dichloromethane (25 mL) and neutralized with 10
% aqueous NaHCO3 solution (10 mL). Organic layer was separated, dried
(over MgSO4) and evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude product was
purified by flash chromatography, using 2% ethyl acetate in hexane as
eluent to afford the desired acetal. Entry7 1H NMR (500 MHz,CDCl3) δ 0.87
(brs, 3H), 1.31 (m, 6H), 1.63 (m, 2H), 3.40 (m, 4H), 3.62 (m, 2H), 3.76
(m, 2H), 4.60 (m, 1H) ppm. 13C NMR (125MHz,CDCl3) δ 103.4, 63.9, 51.2,
32.9, 31.7, 24.4, 22.7, 14.2 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety, Boyer reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Some New Aspects of the Boyer Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
