$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure 1: Acetal Formation: To a stirred substituted
2-bromobenzadehyde (1.0 equiv.) in toluene (50 mL), 1,3-propanediol (1.5
equiv.) and p-toluene sulphonic acid (PTSA) (0.1 equiv.) were added and
the solution was heated at reflux under Dean-Stark conditions for 3
hours. After cooling to room temperature, the reaction mixture was washed
with water, the organic extract dried using MgSO4 and the solvent
evaporated under reduced pressure. The crude compounds were purified by
recrystallisation using a suitable solvent system. From
2-bromobenzadehyde (10.0 g, 54 mmol), 1,3-propanediol (6.16 g, 81 mmol)
and PTSA (0.86 g, 5 mmol). The crude was purified by recrystallisation
from diethyl ether. 2-(2-Bromophenyl)-1,3-dioxane, a white solid, yield
10.47 g, 80%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δH = 7.59 (1H, dd, J = 8.0 and 1.5
Hz, CBrCH), 7.40 (1H, d, J = 8.0 Hz, Ar), 7.20 (1H, t, J = 7.5 Hz, Ar),
7.04 (1H, t of d, J = 8.0 and 1.5 Hz, Ar), 5.63 (1H, s, ArCH), 4.10 (2H,
dd, J = 11.0 and 5.0 Hz, OCH2), 3.85 (2H, t of d, J = 12.5 and 2.0 Hz,
OCH2), 2.16-1.98 (1H, m, OCH2CH2), 1.24 (1H, broad d, J = 13.5 Hz,
OCH2CH2); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δC =137.6, 132.6, 130.4, 128.2, 127.6,
122.4, 100.9, 67.6, 25.7; IR (film / cm-1) ν = 2846 (O-CH-O); HRMS: m/z
(ES) 243.0018, C10H11O2Br [M+H]+ requires 243.0021; mp 53-55 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Dean-Stark conditions used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Intramolecular ester enolate-imine cyclization reactions for the
asymmetric synthesis of polycyclic β-lactams and cyclic β-amino acid
derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Evans, Caroline D.; Mahon, Mary F.; Andrews, Philip C.; Muir, James;
Bull, Steven D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(23), 6276-6279

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME199 STEP1
