$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A mixture of carbonyl compound (1, 2.00 mmol),
pentaerythritol (2, 1.25 mmol), and silica sulfate (100 mg) were mixed
and treated under microwave irradiation 30-300 sec (Table 1). The
progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC. After completion of the
reaction, the mixture was cooled, CH2Cl2 (15 mL) was added to the
reaction mixture and the catalyst was filtered off. The catalyst was
washed with CH2Cl2 (5 mL x 3). Evaporation of the solvent under reduced
pressure afforded the crude product. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel or recrystallized to give diacetals
3. Selected spectral data of some of the products are given below: Table
1, 3l, Entry 12, yield 80% Mp (°C) Found: 168-170; Reported: 170-171[6]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, microwave irradiation, solid-supported catalyst (on
silica is reusable)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of diacetals from aldehydes and ketones with pentaerythritol
catalyzed by silica sulfate under microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jin, Tong-Shou; Wang, Huan-Xin; Wang, Kai-Fang; Li, Tong-Shuang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2004), 34(16), 2993-2999

