$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Acetalization of 16a; Conversion of 16a to 16b. A mixture of dione 16a
(33 mg, 0.1 mmol), ethylene glycol (0.01 mL, 0.20 mmol), PPTS (3 mg), and
benzene (10 mL) was refluxed for 6 h with a Dean-Stark water separator.
Usual workup and removal of solvent furnished a residue, which was
purified by column chromatography using silica gel. Elution with 40%
ethyl acetate-hexane. Mono-acetal 16b (30 mg, 80%). This sample was found
to be identical (mp, IR, and 1H NMR) to the sample 16b derived from
mono-acetal 4b. 16b: mp 279-280 °C; IR (KBr) 1860, 1834, 1779,1736, 1229,
1078 cm-1; 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.55-6.41 (2H, m), 4.09-3.92 (4H,
m), 3.62 (1H, dd, J 1 = 4.4 Hz, J 2 = 2.9 Hz), 3.50 (1H, dd, J 1 = 8.8
Hz, J 2 = 3.3 Hz), 3.42-3.37 (1H, m), 3.32-3.27 (1H, m), 2.70- 2.59 (3H,
m), 2.53-2.44 (2H, m), 2.31-2.23 (1H, m), 1.80 (1H, 1/2 ABq, J = 11.1
Hz), 1.52 (1H, 1/2 ABq, J = 11.1 Hz); 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) δ 212.5,
173.2, 172.6, 134.0, 132.6, 113.1, 65.4, 64.9, 54.2, 51.7, 51.5, 49.3,
44.3, 43.5, 42.0, 40.8, 40.3, 39.8, 39.0, 32.8, 32.4. Anal. Calcd for
C21H18O6: C, 68.85; H, 4.95. Found: C, 68.90; H, 4.98.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Dean-Stark trap used, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Role of Heteroatoms in Diastereofacial Control in Cycloaddition to a
Dissymmetric Cyclohexa-1,3-diene Moiety in a Polycyclic Framework.
Remarkable Stereodirecting Influence of Distal Protective Groups
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Mehta, Goverdhan; Uma, R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2000), 65(6), 1685-1696

