$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Transacetalization with Dimethyl Acetals;
General Procedure Method A: A solution of sucrose (1.57 g, 4.6 mmol),
dimethyl acetal 2 (2.3 mmol) and the catalyst (100 mg) in anhyd DMF (7
mL) was stirred at 25-100°C (Table 1). When all the starting acetal had
reacted (TLC, Et2O/petroleum ether, 1:1), the mixture was filtered and
the filtrate was evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue is then
submitted to flash chromatography using CH2Cl2/acetone/MeOH/H2O
(56:20:20:4) as eluent, providing the sucrose acetal 3. Compound 3g,
yield 80%. 13C NMR: δ = 55.69 (OCH3), 63.25, 64.07 (C-1',6'), 64.78
(C-5), 69.90 (C-6), 71.85 (C-3), 73.92 (C-2), 76.49 (C-4), 80.31 (C-3'),
93.84 (C-5'), 84.95 (C-4), 94.42 (C-1), 103.47 (C-7), 105.52 (C-2),
111.32, 115.65, 120.90 (CHarom)131.03, 148.40, 148.85 (Carom).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Selective synthesis of 4,6-O-alkenylidene and -benzylidene acetals from
unprotected sucrose by lanthanide(III) resin-catalyzed transacetalization
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Porwanski, S.; Salanski, P.; Descotes, G.; Bouchu, A.; Queneau, Y.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2000), (4), 525-528

