$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (1R*,2R*)-2-Dimethoxymethyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-1-naphthol (syn-6).To a
stirred solution of bis-aldehyde (0.44 g, used without purification),
Bu4NBr (0.01 mmol),MS4A (0.8 g) in Et2O (12 mL) was added GeCl2-dioxane
(1.1 mmol) at room temperature. After the mixture was stirred for 2 h, at
room temperature, methanol (20 mL) was added and the resulting solution
was stirred for additional 1 h at room temperature. Then aqueous
NaHCO3(saturated; 50 mL) was added, and the mixture was extracted with
Et2O/hexane (4/1) and the organic layer was dried over MgSO4. The solvent
was evaporated under reduced pressure, and the residue was purified by
flash column chromatography (hexane/ethyl acetate, 95/5) on silicagel
(Fuji Silysia BW-300).The syn isomer was eluted later than anti isomer.
Further purification was performed by recrystallization (hexane).
(1R*,2R*)-2-Dimethoxymethyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydro-1-naphthol, yield white
solid, 80%. mp: 81 °C; IR: (neat) 3413 (OH) cm-1; 1H NMR: (600 MHz,
CDCl3) 7.34-7.31 (m, 1H, 8'-H), 7.22-7.15 (m, 2H, 6'-H, 7'-H),7.12-7.09
(m, 1H, 5'-H), 4.81 (brs, 1H, 1-H), 4.50 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H, 2-CH(OMe)2),
3.42 (s, 3H,OMeA), 3.39 (s, 3H, OMeB), 2.89 (ddd, J = 17.1, 5.4, 2.9 Hz,
1H, 4-HA), 2.76 (ddd, J = 17.1,11.2, 6.6 Hz, 1H, 4-HB), 2.58-2.51 (brs,
1H, OH, D2O-exchangeable), 2.04-1.98 (m, 1H, 2-H), 1.92-1.80 (m, 2H,
3-H2); 1H NMR: (600 MHz, CDCl3, small amount of D2O) 4.79 (d, J = 2.9
Hz,1H, 1-H); 13C NMR: (150 MHz, CDCl3) 137.97 (s, C-8a), 136.60 (s,
C-4a), 129.77 (d, C-8),128.81 (d, C-5), 127.79 (d, C-6), 126.02 (d, C-7),
105.58 (d, 2-CH(OMe)2), 67.58 (d, C-1), 54.04(q, OMeA), 53.54 (q, OMeB),
41.80 (d, C-2), 28.55 (t, C-4), 18.64 (t, C-3); MS: (EI, 70 eV) m/z 204
(M+ - H2O, 1), 190 (M+ - MeOH, 1), 173 (M+ - H2O - OMe, 3), 130 (M+ -
C(OMe)2 - H2O, 61),129 (M+ - CH(OMe)2 - H2O, 23), 75 (CH(OMe)2, 100), 71
(M+ - CH(OMe)2 - C6H4, 20); HRMS:(EI, 70 eV) calcd for C13H16O2 204.1150
(M+ - H2O) found for m/z 204.1153. Anal. Calcd for C13H16O2: C, 70.24; H,
8.16. Found C, 70.06; H, 8.36.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, molecular sieves added
