$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of n-hexanal (0.100 mL, 0.718 mmol) in PhMe (3.00 mL) was
added benzyloxytrimethylsilane (0.310 mL, 1.58 mmol). After stirring for
10 min at -78 °C, trimethylsilyl trifluoromethanesulfonate (13.0 μL, 71.9
μmol) was added. After stirring for 19.5 h at -40 °C, the reaction was
quenched with pyridine (23.0 μL, 0.286 mmol). The mixture was warmed to
room temperature and saturated NaHCO3 (1.50 mL) was added. The aqueous
layer was extracted with PhMe (3×3.00 mL). The combined organic layers
were concentrated in vacuo. The resulting residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (n-hexane - ethyl acetate = 1 : 1) to give
the acetal n. Colorless oil, yield (0.171 g, 0.573 mmol, 80%). Rf value :
0.64 (n-hexane - ethyl acetate = 4 : 1). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm)
7.41-7.27 (10H, m), 4.76 (1H, t, J = 5.7 Hz), 4.68 (2H, d, J = 11.5 Hz),
4.58 (2H, d, J = 11.5 Hz), 1.84-1.70 (2H, m), 1.47-1.37 (2H, m),
1.37-1.24 (4H, m), 0.96-0.84 (3H, m); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm)
138.4, 128.4, 127.8, 127.5, 102.3, 67.1, 33.2, 31.6, 24.4, 22.6, 14.0;
HRMS (m/z) : 297.1856 [M-H]+ ; calcd for C20H25O2 : 297.1855; IR (cm-1) :
2956, 2925, 2863, 1453, 1113, 1026, 733, 697.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM syn-Selective Kobayashi Aldol Reaction Using Acetals
