$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 64-17-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Selective Acetalization
of Benzaldehyde vs. Acetophenone with Triethylorthoformate To a
magnetically stirred solution of benzaldehyde (3 mmol), acetophenone (3
mmol), (EtO)3CH (10 mmol) in absolute alcohol 10 mL of reflux was added
TiO2/SO42- (100 mg). After completion of the reaction, the catalyst was
filtered off and washed with Et2O, and the filtrate was washed with
brine(2 x 15 mL) and dried (MgSO4). The organic layer was concentrated
under reduced pressure. The mixture was separated by silical gel column
chromatography to afford phenylmethanediol diethyl ether in 96% yield and
the acetophenone was almost quantitatively recovered. Table 2, Entry 16,
yield 95%; yield 2%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A highly efficient and chemoselective method for acetalization of
carbonyl compounds catalyzed by TiO2/SO42- solid superacid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
